lot of new territory, before we do that though,&nbsp;
open source, just for people who may not have&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:34.240 --> 00:03:39.320
familiarity with that term, what does that mean?
Matt Mullenweg: Normally when you sign up for&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.320 --> 00:03:44.360
software, you click through that license that no&nbsp;
one ever reads. Ours actually has Easter eggs in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:44.360 --> 00:03:47.680
